-- title:
--   Generic crude depth guard for recursions with shrinking children
-- statement:
--   Let $A : \mathbb N \to \mathbb R$, $E, L \ge 0$, $T > 0$, $s, m \ge 2$. Suppose that every $e \ge T$ has a list of at most $s$ children $c$ with $m c \le (m-1) e$ and $A(e) \le E + \sum_c A(c)$, and that $A(e) \le L$ for $e < T$. Then for every $e$
--
--   $$A(e) \le (E + L)\left(2 s^{\max(0,\ m(\log e - \log T) + 1)} - 1\right).$$
--
--   This is the crude bound on the size of a recursion tree whose children shrink by the factor $(m-1)/m$; it is the common core of the depth-guard estimates below.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem R6.guard_gen (E L T : ℝ) (s m : ℕ) (A : ℕ → ℝ) (hm : 2 ≤ m) (hs : 2 ≤ s) (hE : 0 ≤ E)
--       (hL : 0 ≤ L) (hT : 0 < T)
--       (hrec : ∀ e : ℕ, T ≤ e → ∃ cs : List ℕ, cs.length ≤ s ∧ (∀ c ∈ cs, m * c ≤ (m - 1) * e) ∧
--         A e ≤ E + (cs.map A).sum)
--       (hleaf : ∀ e : ℕ, (e : ℝ) < T → A e ≤ L) :
--       ∀ e : ℕ, A e ≤ (E + L) * (2 * (s : ℝ) ^ (max 0 (m * (Real.log e - Real.log T) + 1)) - 1)
--   ```
